      "message": "Thanks for looking into this. We hit the same crash downstream and can\nconfirm the root cause: b-\u003etrace_handle refers to a record in the pool\nof the thread that traced the buffer, but dispatch_pcap_trace() looks\nthe index up in the pool of the current thread. In our case, packets\nwere handed off from a worker to the main thread, whose trace pool is\nalways NULL because it polls no NICs.\n\nIt also reproduces with stock VPP: 2 workers,\n\"set interface handoff pg0 workers 1\", a pg stream on worker 0 and\n\"pcap dispatch trace on max 1000 buffer-trace pg-input 10\". Worker 1\nthen gets SIGSEGV at address 0x0.\n\nSome comments inline. In short: pool_is_free_index() instead of the\nNULL checks, no barrier sync/release, and a shorter code comment.\n\nA regression test would be good, too. The test below fails (VPP crash)\nwithout the fix and passes with it. Feel free to add it to\ntest/test_pcap.py:\n\n    @unittest.skipIf(\n        \"dispatch-trace\" in config.excluded_plugins, \"Exclude dispatch trace plugin tests\"\n    )\n    class TestPcapDispatchTraceHandoff(VppTestCase):\n        \"\"\"Pcap dispatch trace with worker handoff\"\"\"\n\n        vpp_worker_count \u003d 2\n\n        @classmethod\n        def setUpClass(cls):\n            super(TestPcapDispatchTraceHandoff, cls).setUpClass()\n\n            cls.create_pg_interfaces(range(2))\n            for i in cls.pg_interfaces:\n                i.admin_up()\n                i.config_ip4()\n                i.resolve_arp()\n\n        @classmethod\n        def tearDownClass(cls):\n            for i in cls.pg_interfaces:\n                i.unconfig_ip4()\n                i.admin_down()\n\n            super(TestPcapDispatchTraceHandoff, cls).tearDownClass()\n\n        def test_dispatch_trace_handoff(self):\n            \"\"\"Dispatch trace of buffers traced on another worker\"\"\"\n            pcap_file \u003d \"/tmp/dispatch_handoff.pcap\"\n            if os.path.exists(pcap_file):\n                os.remove(pcap_file)\n\n            # pg-input traces the packets on worker 0, the packets are then\n            # handed off to worker 1, which has no trace records of its own\n            self.vapi.cli(\"set interface handoff pg0 workers 1\")\n            self.vapi.cli(\n                \"pcap dispatch trace on max 1000 file dispatch_handoff.pcap \"\n                \"buffer-trace pg-input 10\"\n            )\n\n            pkts \u003d [\n                Ether(src\u003dself.pg0.remote_mac, dst\u003dself.pg0.local_mac)\n                / IP(src\u003dself.pg0.remote_ip4, dst\u003dself.pg1.remote_ip4)\n                / UDP(sport\u003d1234, dport\u003d2345)\n                / Raw(b\"\\xa5\" * 100)\n            ] * 5\n            self.send_and_expect(self.pg0, pkts, self.pg1, worker\u003d0, trace\u003dFalse)\n            self.assertIn(\"HANDED-OFF: from thread 1\", self.vapi.cli(\"show trace\"))\n\n            self.vapi.cli(\"pcap dispatch trace off\")\n            self.vapi.cli(\"set interface handoff pg0 workers 1 disable\")\n            self.assertTrue(os.path.exists(pcap_file))\n            os.remove(pcap_file)",
