      "side": 1,
      "message": "Suggest a shorter comment. The debugging details (DISP-TRACE-HANDOFF\nevidence) are already in the commit message.\n\nAlso, this code never reads the pool of another thread. It reads its\nown pool with an index that belongs to another thread. And the loss is\nnot quite zero: records on the new thread have no trace text until a\nnode there adds its own trace (vlib_add_trace() then moves the trace to\nthis thread, with a HANDED-OFF entry). For example:\n\n      /*\n       * Trace records live in per-thread pools. A buffer handed off\n       * from another thread still refers to a record in the pool of\n       * that thread, and a buffer traced before \u0027clear trace\u0027 refers\n       * to a freed record. Only records of this thread\u0027s pool can be\n       * used here, see also vlib_add_trace_inline().\n       */",
      "revId": "26a3a7a017762dbe28bd09b7732305018ba75b8d",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
